  "subject": {
    "id": "small-shop-full-public-population-proof",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Run the complete Small Shop dataset through the public population, history, replay, query, and trace path.",
  "why": "The earlier five-stage showcase proved the domain story through a private direct change-set assembler, while later public seams were proven on smaller slices. This conformance fixture preserves that historical evidence and expresses the same full dataset as five canonical adopter-authored population plans. One public-facade runner admits those plans around one additive ontology revision, reopens one append-only history, reproduces the same nine-record current graph, retains the superseded tenth record, and verifies every record back to exact plan, derivation, source, and mapping bytes. It adds no protocol rule, mapping DSL, universal domain-history model, Event population, Semantic Re-entry, stable wire, or release claim."
}
